## Code style

@.claude/instructions/coding-guidelines.md
@.claude/instructions/security.md

- New components must be standalone. No new NgModules.
- Modern control flow: `@if`, `@for`, `@switch`, not `*ngIf` / `*ngFor`.
- Component selector prefix `app-` (kebab-case); directive prefix `app` (camelCase).
- Styling: <utility classes first; a stylesheet only when utilities cannot express it>.
  Design system: `DESIGN.md`; colour and contrast rules: the `accessibility` skill.

## Git: branches, commits, releases

- Branch names: `feature/PROJ-123-description`.
- Never push directly to `<integration-branch>` or `<release-branch>`. PRs target
  `<integration-branch>`.
- Commit format:
  - **Ticket work**: `[PROJ-123] Description`. Ticket-prefixed commits have no conventional
    type and never trigger a release.
  - **Everything else**: conventional `type(scope): subject`.
- **Release trap**: on `<integration-branch>`, semantic-release cuts a release from the
  conventional commits. If the config maps `docs:`, `chore:`, `test:`, `ci:`, `style:` and
  `build:` to a **patch** and `refactor:` to a **minor**, every "harmless" commit consumes a
  version. Use the scope `no-release` (`docs(no-release): ...`) when a change must not.
- Pipeline tokens (your own list, e.g. `[skip ci]`, `[skip test]`, `[e2e:all]`,
  `[e2e:<domain>]`); details in the `<run-skill>` skill.

## Pre-push quality gate

The `pre-push` hook enforces automatically:

1. The linter must pass on all changed source files.
2. Every changed `*.component.ts` (and `.service.ts`, `.directive.ts`, ...) must have a
   sibling `*.spec.ts`.
3. Unit tests run on affected files with coverage; global thresholds of
   `<coverage-threshold>` (80%) for statements, branches, functions and lines.

Bypass (`git push --no-verify`) is for hotfixes only; document the rationale in the PR
description. A hook in `.claude/settings.json` stops Claude from using it at all.

## Testing notes

- Unit test config: `<jest-config>` for the shell; each app has its own. Coverage output:
  `coverage/<app>/`.
- E2E always runs against the **mock server**, never a live environment. E2E intercepts the
  feature-flag file; fixture patterns in `<e2e-support-dir>`.
- Test-layer selection and what evidence counts: the `validation-and-qa` skill.

## Session hooks (already automated, don't duplicate)

`.claude/settings.json` blocks edits to protected files (`.env`, lockfiles,
`<bot-managed-config>`), blocks credential-shaped content, blocks `git push --no-verify` and
pushes to protected branches, blocks commits that stage a submodule pointer by accident, and
auto-runs the formatter on written source files. Don't hand-format, and don't try to edit
those protected files. Scripts and their tests: `.claude/hooks/`.
